# Luminary marker — 1.9.22 release
- date: 2026-11-07
- branch: release-1.9.22
- lead: jony-ive
- supporting: [michael-feathers]

## What each lens caught

- jony-ive (lead) — material honesty. A character grid is not a bitmap. The
  old mark asked terminal cells to behave like pixels, and they do not: line
  spacing is the viewer's setting, and font coverage is the font's business.
  The cure was to stop pretending and use the alphabet, which every font has.
- michael-feathers — the grid is data that corrupts silently. A paste from a
  figlet generator can carry a Unicode dash, and an edit can pad one row and
  not its neighbours. Neither shows on the author's own machine. The sibling
  tests assert the character set and the row widths mechanically for that
  reason, and they were rewritten rather than dropped when the grid changed.
